This manuscript continues the exact free Dirac construction in the recovered v0.49.0 physics handoff. It supplies proofs at the level of mathematical analysis for the generator of the constructed unitary group, for strong resolvent convergence of the centered Fourier multiplier family, and for a global second order spacing estimate under third order Fourier regularity. The results are stated for the same fixed torus coefficient space as the preceding formal work.

\textbf{Not a new Lean certification.} The v0.49.0 source and its verification reports were inspected. A proposed Block 50 finite cutoff Lean interface is included with the release, but the current execution environment does not contain the pinned Lean toolchain or Mathlib. The new Lean module was not compiled. The theorems in this manuscript are analytic proofs and should not be represented as newly checked Lean declarations.

\textbf{Not a new physical prediction.} The spatial background is a flat three torus. The free four spinor construction neither supplies dynamic gauge fields nor a gravitational continuum limit. The centered symbol acts on an unchanged infinite Fourier index set, not on a sampled finite lattice with changing Nyquist scale.

\begin{center}\color{cyan}\rule{.95\linewidth}{.65pt}\end{center}
\textbf{Result map.} The unitary group is shown to have generator $-iH$ on precisely $\Dn(H)$. The physical torus evolution therefore agrees with the spectral exponential of the self adjoint Hamiltonian already transported to that space. The centered generators converge to $H$ on its graph domain and converge in the strong resolvent sense. For fields with a finite third order spatial Fourier moment, the centered propagator error on $|t|\le T$ is bounded by $T h^2/6$ times that moment norm.

