\midrule
Theorem & Proved from the assumptions printed next to the statement.\\
Conditional theorem & Exact after a finite-depth, regularity, branch, or spectral-headroom hypothesis is imposed.\\
Controlled diagnostic & A deterministic calculation that tests a declared model or fixed parameter set.\\
Model proposition & A candidate physical completion that is not forced by the projector axioms.\\
Open problem & A required derivation or external validation that is not completed here.\\
\bottomrule
\end{longtable}

\begin{statusbox}[Central boundary]
The projector and refinement identities remain mathematically meaningful after the cosmological benchmark fails a production-control test.  What changes is the physical status of the dark-sector branch.  Its late-time transport remains a calculation from a prescribed normalized distribution.  That distribution is not yet the output of a controlled backreacting crossing.
\end{statusbox}

